Using Incrementing die system

Whenever a CHARACTER rolls the highest value on their die it CRITS.
Everytime a character CRITS on a skill check that skill goes up a die type. They then roll the new die and add the results together for the current skill check. 
Ex: A player rolls a BRAWL check, they have a d4 for the stat and roll a 4, they now roll a d6 and roll a 2, adding that value to the previous roll for a total check of 6. That player now has a d6 for BRAWL.

Everyone starts at a d4 for all stats

stats being //under work still

Brawl - Checks to harm others physically
Charisma - Checks to be percieved a certain way
Sneak - Checks to operate without being seen
Stunts - Checks to move rapidly or evade
Tech - Checks to operate machinery
Tough - Checks to protect self from injury
Wit - Checks to discern and/or inspire
Instinct - Checks to sense danger

Stand creation rather than being the stand stats youll select a series of modifiers that will alter how your stand operates
starting with the base of: Long range Humanoid stand - range of 50 meters, no other modifiers

Modifiers:
Modifiers will affect the stands range, bonuses to rolls, and stand abilities
ex. Gain a +5 to all brawl checks involving your stand, reduce this stands range to 2 meters

INJURY
THERE ARE 3 INJURY LEVELS
SUPERFICIAL, SEVERE, ADRENALIZED
WHEN A PLAYER FAILS A CHECK TO AVOID DAMAGE BY 5 OR MORE, THEY TAKE AN INJURY LEVEL
SUPERFICIAL
  -Your character gets an injury that looks badass
  -No reprecussions
SEVERE
  -Your character recieves a debilitating injury
  -A player with this injury level must spend double the amount of Tokens
ADRENALIZED
  -Your character is grievously wounded
  -A player with this injury level recieves 10 Tokens. The next time this character fails a check to avoid injury, they become either Incapacitated or Dead, 
  depending on the attackers intention
